} :answer-field/id #uuid "42f6efb1-acc1-594f-9863-9843b604f60e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514255}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "34621fcb-1a0d-5d3e-9880-09e09830a08f" :question/math-academy-id "q-2024" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt{x}={x}^{1/2}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{1}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{1/2+1}}{(\\frac{1}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3/2}}{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3/2})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3/2-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{1/2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514390 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "877168ac-4c34-57ba-a846-5362369f5757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{5}{x}^{3/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513885} {:answer/id #uuid "943d70e7-e52b-597e-9871-44857a8a7ae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}{x}^{5/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513915} {:answer/id #uuid "c6b24cd8-5808-5ff4-8dd5-6d0e70ccaa9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{5}{x}^{5/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514052} {:answer/id #uuid "e25dd75d-4458-58ea-a630-3ccbc3fecb7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}{x}^{3/2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514125} {:answer/id #uuid "e355f008-e331-